## 3. SPI and pipeline changes

The handler now receives the matched entries, since that's usually what the business API needs:

```java
public interface TopicHandler<T> {
    // ...unchanged...
    Mono<Void> onMatch(T payload, String nationalCode, List<RedisEntry> entries);
    default Mono<Void> onNoMatch(T payload, String nationalCode) { return Mono.empty(); }
}
```

```java
// in KafkaIngestionPipeline.process(...)
return lookup.findAll(nc)
        .collectList()
        .flatMap(entries -> entries.isEmpty()
                ? handler.onNoMatch(payload, nc)
                : handler.onMatch(payload, nc, entries));
```

Example handler usage:

```java
@Override
public Mono<Void> onMatch(LoanRequestEvent p, String nc, List<RedisEntry> entries) {
    var body = Map.of(
        "requestId", p.requestId(),
        "nationalCode", nc,
        "profiles", entries.stream().map(RedisEntry::value).toList()   // or parse each value to a DTO
    );
    return api.post("loan-api", "/loans/flag", body);
}
```

If a handler only cares about certain keys, it can filter on `entry.key()` (e.g. `startsWith("customer:")`) — the pattern stays generic in config.

